mask 00000000 00100000 the EE kernel's area: empty in the port, which has no kernel
mask 00217ee0 00000420 the debug CPU meter's readings of the EE timer (meter.c reads T0_COUNT directly); the port's timers are plain memory
mask 00218380 00000200 the pads' DMA buffers (scePadPortOpen), which the IOP rewrites every vblank; the game reads them only through scePadRead
mask 005b5870 00001b20 libdma, libpad, libcdvd and libmc .data
mask 005b73c8 00000008 newlib's stdio state in _reent (__sdidinit, __cleanup): the EE's debug printf initialises stdio; the port's C library has no newlib stdio
mask 005b7568 00000114 newlib's stdio state in _reent (__sglue and the three FILEs __sf), for the same reason
mask 005b7b00 00000004 the kernel library's tty state (glue.c)
mask 005b7b08 000016f8 the kernel, SIF, file I/O and IOP-load libraries' .data
mask 005ce100 00000148 the kernel's argv for main(), which the port's host does not fill
mask 005e2100 00000028 the sound driver's RPC client (sceSifClientData): libsif keeps its IOP-side state there; the game reads only serve
mask 00622180 00006bec the replaced libraries' .bss: libdma to deci2 and the exception register save area
mask 01fe0000 00020000 the main thread's stack (crt0: SetupThread(_gp, 0x1fe0000, 0x20000)); the port's stack is in its own area
ptrmask 005cc928 4 4 3c 640 00000000 0 ffff 0 0 BG_WORK.CellAddr: BgWork_Initial copies it from a BGINIT_ARG that BG_LoadTexture never sets, so the EE stores a leftover stack word and the port zero (it zero-fills locals); nothing reads it
ptrmask 005cc920 dc 4 11c 160 005cc970 7 4 2 80 CHARACTER_WORK.RHitBackx of stage 7's background objects (idno 0x80): BG_Init creates them with CREATE_ARG flag 0x65, which copies tx and ty, and never sets ty, so the EE stores a leftover stack word and the port zero; the rest of the trace shows nothing reads it
